#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:100
msgid "**Configure the integration in Mattermost**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:102
msgid ""
"Confirm whether your Mattermost deployment has a ``github`` user account."
" If it exists, that account posts GitHub messages in channels by default,"
" and the messages won't include a BOT tag. You can change this account "
"behavior to include a BOT tag by using one of the following methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:104
msgid ""
"Convert the user account to a bot using :ref:`mmctl user convert "
"<administration-guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool:mmctl user "
"convert>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:105
msgid ""
"Change the existing ``github`` username to something else. A new bot "
"account called ``github`` is created the Mattermost server is restarted "
"when the :ref:`enable bot account creation <administration-"
"guide/configure/integrations-configuration-settings:enable bot account "
"creation>` configuration setting is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:107
msgid ""
"In Mattermost, go to **System Console > Plugins > GitHub** and configure "
"the following settings, then select **Save**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:109
msgid ""
"Enter the **GitHub OAuth Client ID** and **GitHub OAuth Client Secret** "
"obtained during registration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:110
msgid ""
"(Optional) **GitHub Organization**: Lock the integration to GitHub "
"organizations by specifying a comma seperated list of your GitHub "
"organizations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:111
msgid ""
"(GitHub Enterprise Only): Set **Enterprise Base URL** and **Enterprise "
"Upload URL** values to your GitHub Enterprise URLs, e.g. "
"``https://github.example.com``. These values are often the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:112
msgid ""
"(Mattermost desktop app only) **Display Notification Counters in Left "
"Sidebar**: Display or hide GitHub notification counters in the Mattermost"
" sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:113
msgid ""
"(Optional) **Enable Private Repositories**: Enable the ability to work "
"with private repositories. Affected users are notified once private "
"repositories are enabled, and must reconnect their GitHub accounts to "
"gain access to private repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:114
msgid ""
"(Optional) **Connect to private Repositories by default**: Connect to "
"private GitHub repositories by default, when private repositories are "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:115
msgid ""
"(Optional) **Enable Code Previews**: Expand permalinks to GitHub files "
"with previews. You can can enable public repositories, public and private"
" repositories, or disable this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:116
msgid ""
"(Optional) **Enable Webhook Event Logging**: Log webhook events when log "
"level set to DEBUG by enabling the  option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:117
msgid ""
"(Optional) **Show Author in commit notification**: Show commit author "
"instead of committer in GitHub push event notifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:120
msgid "Upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:122
msgid ""
"We recommend updating this integration as new versions are released. "
"Generally, updates are seamless and don't interrupt the user experience "
"in Mattermost. Visit the `Releases page <https://github.com/mattermost"
"/mattermost-plugin-github/releases>`__ for the latest release, available "
"releases, and compatibiilty considerations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:125
msgid "Enable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:127
msgid ""
"Once you setup the integration, notify your teams that they can `connect "
"their GitHub accounts to Mattermost <#connect-a-github-account-to-"
"mattermost>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:130
msgid "Use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:132
msgid ""
"Users who want to use GitHub interconnectivity must connect their GitHub "
"account to Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:134
msgid ""
"Once connected, you'll receive direct messages from the GitHub bot in "
"Mattermost when someone mentions you, requests a review, comments on, "
"modifies one of your pull requests/issues (includes adding labels or "
"reopening the issue), or assigns you to an issue on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:137
msgid "Connect a GitHub account to Mattermost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:139
msgid ""
"In Mattermost, run the ``/github connect`` slash command in any "
"Mattermost channel to link your Mattermost account with your GitHub "
"account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:141
msgid ""
"Once connected, run the ``/github help`` slash command to see what you "
"can do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:144
msgid "Get started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:146
msgid "Here are some common slash commands you can get started with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:148
msgid ""
"Run the ``/github subscriptions add`` slash command to subscribe a "
"Mattermost channel to receive notifications for new pull requests, "
"issues, branch creation, and more in a GitHub repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:150
msgid ""
"For example, to post notifications for issues, issue comments, and pull "
"requests matching the label **Help Wanted** from the ``mattermost"
"/mattermost-server`` GitHub repository, use: ``/github subscriptions add "
"mattermost/mattermost-server --features "
"issues,pulls,issue_comments,label:\"Help Wanted\"``. The following flags "
"are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:152
msgid ""
"``--features``: A comma-delimited list of one or more of: issues, pulls, "
"pulls_merged, pulls_created, pushes, creates, deletes, issue_creations, "
"issue_comments, pull_reviews, releases, workflow_success, "
"workflow_failure, discussions, discussion_comments, label:\"labelname\". "
"Defaults to ``pulls,issues,creates,deletes``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:153
msgid ""
"``--exclude-org-member``: The events triggered by organization members "
"that won't be delivered. It will be locked to the organization configured"
" and only works for users whose membership is public. Organization "
"members and collaborators are not the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:154
msgid ""
"``--include-only-org-members``: events triggered only by organization "
"members will be delivered. It will be locked to the organization provided"
" in the plugin configuration and it will only work for users whose "
"membership is public. Note that organization members and collaborators "
"are not the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:155
msgid ""
"``--render-style``: Notifications are delivered in the specified style "
"(for example, the body of a pull request will not be displayed). "
"Supported values are ``collapsed``, ``skip-body``, or ``default`` (which "
"is the same as omitting the flag)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:156
msgid ""
"``--exclude``: A comma-separated list of the repositories to exclude from"
" getting the subscription notifications like ``mattermost/mattermost-"
"server``. Only supported for subscriptions to an organization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:158
msgid ""
"Run the ``/github todo`` slash command to get a message with items to do "
"in GitHub, including a list of unread messages and pull requests awaiting"
" your review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:160
msgid ""
"Run the ``/github settings`` slash command to update your settings for "
"notifications and daily reminders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:162
msgid ""
"Run the ``/github mute`` slash command to manage muted GitHub users. You "
"won't receive notifications for comments in your pull requests and issues"
" from muted users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:164
msgid ""
"Run the ``/github default-repo`` slash command to set a default "
"repository for the current channel. This repository will be auto-filled "
"in the Create GitHub Issue modal for convenience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:167
msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:170
msgid "How do I connect a repository instead of an organization?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:172
msgid ""
"Set up your GitHub webhook from the repository instead of the "
"organization. Notifications and subscriptions will then be sent only for "
"repositories you create webhooks for. The reminder and ``/github todo`` "
"searches the whole organization, but only show items assigned to you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:175
msgid "How do I send notifications when a certain label is applied?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:177
msgid ""
"If you want to send notifications to a Mattermost channel when "
"**Severity/Critical** label is applied to any issue in the ``mattermost"
"/mattermost-plugin-github`` repository, run the following slash command "
"to subscribe to these notifications: ``/github subscriptions add "
"mattermost/mattermost-plugin-github issues,label:\"Severity/Critical\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:180
msgid "How does the integration save user data for each connected GitHub user?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/github.rst:182
msgid ""
"GitHub user tokens are AES-encrypted with an **At Rest Encryption Key** "
"generated in Mattermost. Once encrypted, the tokens are saved in the "
"``PluginKeyValueStore`` table in your Mattermost database."
msgstr ""

